<DANMILLER> **********
<DANMILLER> Topic 3         Tue Mar 22, 1988
<DANMILLER> G.SHAW1                      at 06:19 PST
<DANMILLER> Sub: A SIGForth is starting in ACM - Help!
<DANMILLER> A SIG for Forth is starting in ACM.  This will give Forth 
professionals a
<DANMILLER> resource for support in selling and using Forth professionally.  
Activity is
<DANMILLER> needed to make it successful.  Look here for info...
<DANMILLER> **********
<DANMILLER> ----------
<DANMILLER> Category 5,  Topic 3
<DANMILLER> Message 1         Tue Mar 22, 1988
<DANMILLER> G.SHAW1                      at 06:21 PST
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER> I'm in the process of starting a SIG for Forth within ACM (SIGForth)
.  ACM
<DANMILLER> membership will not be required to join.  A sister effort will 
start in IEEE
<DANMILLER> later this year.  I need help on several fronts:
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      1) Officers for the SIG.  Chairman, Vice-chairman and
<DANMILLER>      Sec/Treas.  I'm willing to chair or vice-chair, but I need
<DANMILLER>      more bodies to run it.  Candidates must be or become ACM
<DANMILLER>      members to be officers.  You must also be a computer
<DANMILLER>      professional to be a voting member (programmer, Dp manager,
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      etc).  The work load is not great, but you must be sure you
<DANMILLER>      have the time and will do what you've agreed to do.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      2) Advertising/announcing the existence of the SIG.  We'd
<DANMILLER>      love to co-op or ride in a vendor's mailing.  ***Vendors***
<DANMILLER>      contact me asap.  Announcements at FIG chapter is needed.
<DANMILLER>      Etc.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      3) We need help collecting and analyzing information
<DANMILLER>      collected/to be collected from our projects (see SIGFORTH
<DANMILLER>      file).  Call me so I can connect people with similar
<DANMILLER>      interests.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      4) We need material for our newsletter.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      5) We need *****members****!!!  Send me your name and address
<DANMILLER>      so that we can notify you when the SIG is underway.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      6) I'm trying to get the creating paper work wrapped up by
<DANMILLER>      the end of March.  As much input ASAP so I can finish the 1st
<DANMILLER>      year budget would be appreciated.  If nothing else, let me
<DANMILLER>      know if you would become a member so I can project a member
<DANMILLER>      count.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      7) We're planning on holding a conference in Texas (probably
<DANMILLER>      Austin) next February.  Would you attend?  Would another
<DANMILLER>      location in that region be better.  Please let us know.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>      8) I need petitions from voting ACM members stating "I
<DANMILLER>      support the formation of a SIG for Forth (SIGForth) within
<DANMILLER>      ACM to promote the use of Forth professionally" with their
<DANMILLER>      ACM# and signature.  As many as possible ASAP.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER> Please call me at (415) 276-5953 or contact me on GEnie if that is 
more
<DANMILLER> convenient.  My mailing address is PO Box 3471, Hayward, CA 
94540-3471.  This
<DANMILLER> SIG is for us, by us.  I appreciate your support.
<DANMILLER> -
<DANMILLER>    George Shaw
<DANMILLER> ----------
